  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "dWza8SUMi/92mvy+l1eUFHf7Noc=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T13:23:19.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "# powa-revenue-distribution model captures epoch-based token revenue sharing\n\n## Purpose\n\nModels a revenue distribution system where revenue is split proportionally across multiple epochs, each containing investor tokens (iPOWA) and contributor tokens (cPOWA). Each epoch has a weight factor that determines its share of total revenue. The document model provides an off-chain configuration, simulation, and audit layer for what ultimately deploys as Solidity smart contracts.\n\nSource: [NicWickman/powa](https://github.com/NicWickman/powa)\n\n## State Schema\n\n**Core entities (from requirements, not yet architected):**\n\n- **Epoch** \u2014 index, iPOWA supply, cPOWA supply, weight factor, status (DRAFT/APPROVED/DEPLOYED/RETIRED), on-chain addresses (post-deploy), label\n- **Revenue Configuration** \u2014 total amount, revenue token identifier, distribution date\n- **Distribution Record** \u2014 epoch reference, deposited amount, iPOWA/cPOWA distributed amounts, dust, tx hash, timestamp\n- **User Holding** (simulation, likely local scope) \u2014 iPOWA/cPOWA balances per epoch, computed claimable\n- **Claim Target** \u2014 account address, target contract address, target type\n\nGlobal scope: epochs, revenue config, distribution records\nLocal scope (candidate): user holding simulations\n\n## Modules\n\nProposed module split (deferred to Architect):\n\n1. **EpochManagement** \u2014 create, edit, reorder epochs; status lifecycle transitions\n2. **RevenueConfiguration** \u2014 set total revenue, denomination, schedule\n3. **DistributionTracking** \u2014 record deposits, per-epoch actuals, dust, claim events\n4. **HolderSimulation** \u2014 define user holdings, compute claimable amounts\n5. **TargetConfiguration** \u2014 register claim destinations per account\n\n## Key Design Decisions\n\n- Off-chain model represents the *business view* (epoch config, allocations, claims), not Solidity internals (accumulators, rewardDebt)\n- Status lifecycle (DRAFT\u2192APPROVED\u2192DEPLOYED\u2192RETIRED) provides a governance gate before irreversible on-chain deployment\n- Computed fields (weighted supply, revenue share, claimable) may be derived at render time rather than stored \u2014 Architect decides\n- This is a **new functional zone** (Token Economics / Revenue Distribution) \u2014 does not extend any existing Powerhouse model\n- Maximum 20 epochs per document (mirrors on-chain gas limit policy)\n\n---\n\nRelevant Notes:\n- [[epochs distribute revenue proportionally by weighted token supply]]\n- [[masterchef accumulator pattern enables per-token revenue tracking]]\n- [[powa document model bridges on-chain contracts with off-chain governance]]\n\nTopics:\n- [[ecosystem map]]\n- [[schema design]]",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T13:23:19.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T13:23:19.000Z"
    }
  },
